---
source: crates/wormhole-cli/src/cli_tests.rs
expression: help
---
Wormhole exposes local services through one or more secure tunnel providers

Usage: wormhole [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  http         Expose a local HTTP service
  tcp          Expose a local TCP service
  run          Run a command and expose its listening port
  up           Start services from wormhole.toml
  down         Stop project services or endpoint identifiers
  ls           List active endpoints
  status       Show daemon status
  inspect      Inspect one captured HTTP request
  requests     List or manage captured HTTP requests
  replay       Replay one captured request
  interfaces   List discovered interface aliases
  remote       Manage named Wormhole remotes
  key          Manage the client identity key
  doctor       Run structured health checks
  daemon       Manage the per-user daemon
  completions  Generate shell completions
  share        Create an expiring share link
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --json
          Emit stable JSON instead of human-readable output

      --config <PATH>
          Override the global configuration file

  -q, --quiet
          Suppress nonessential diagnostics

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase diagnostic verbosity (repeat for trace logging)

  -h, --help
          Print help

  -V, --version
          Print version
